messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: schematron.c
Line: 1953
Function: xmlSchematronValidateDoc
Bug type: use-after-free
CWE: CWE-416
Explanation: xmlSchematronRunTest() (line 1941) calls xmlSchematronReportSuccess(), which can trigger user callbacks (xmlRaiseError/xmlSchematronReportOutput) that may free the current node 'cur' or the document. On returning, the code proceeds to 'cur = xmlSchematronNextNode(cur);' at line 1953, dereferencing 'cur' (via cur->children etc.) and causing a use-after-free if 'cur' was freed in the callback.

Source context:
